---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { REPO_URL } from "../../lib/github";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout currentSlug="building" title="Building from source" description="Build it yourself, desktop and Android.">
  <p>
    You need stable Rust from <a href="https://rustup.rs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">rustup</a>
    (<code>rust-toolchain.toml</code> picks the rest) and git 2.38 or later. On a Mac, the Command Line Tools are enough;
    you don't need Xcode.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={"git clone " + REPO_URL + ".git\ncd corvene\ncargo run -p corvene"} />

  <h2 id="linux">Linux</h2>
  <p>Install these first (Debian and Ubuntu names):</p>
  <CodeBlock
    code="sudo apt install clang mold pkg-config libxcb1-dev libxkbcommon-dev libxkbcommon-x11-dev libwayland-dev libfontconfig-dev libfreetype-dev libvulkan-dev"
  />

  <h2 id="checks">Before you send a change</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={"cargo fmt --check\ncargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings\ncargo test --workspace"} />
  <p>
    CI runs the same three. If you changed something on screen, run the <a href={`${base}/docs/parity`}>parity harness</a>
    for it too.
  </p>

  <h2 id="full">Full edition</h2>
  <p>Full compiles every tree-sitter grammar in. Fetch the grammar sources once, then build with the feature:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={"python3 tools/ts-queries/fetch.py\ncargo build --release -p corvene --features full"} />
  <p>It takes a good while longer than a normal build.</p>

  <h2 id="android">Android</h2>
  <p>
    Both apps need the Android SDK and NDK, a JDK 17 or later, and <code>cargo install cargo-ndk</code>. The first build
    also cross-compiles the git, OpenSSH and Git LFS the apps ship with, which needs make, perl and Go.
  </p>
  <p>Corvene Legacy:</p>
  <CodeBlock code="ABIS=arm64-v8a packaging/android/build.sh debug foss" />
  <p>The new Corvene app, once <code>packaging/android/git/build.sh</code> has built the bundled git:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={"cd android\n./gradlew :app:installFossDebug"} />
  <p><code>android/README.md</code> has the rest, including how to run it on a phone.</p>

  <h2 id="code">Finding things</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href={`${base}/docs/architecture`}>architecture page</a> lists the crates. Dialogs, foldouts and menus keep
    GitHub Desktop's names, so its <code>ConfirmDiscardChanges</code> is <code>dialogs::confirm_discard_changes</code> here.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
